From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
Date: Sat, 4 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] esp32c6: resolve boot image offset from otadata at load time

When a Zephyr image is delivered through ESP-IDF-style OTA (the C6 keeps
the stock 2nd-stage bootloader + otadata), it may physically live in
either ota_0 or ota_1. The link-time PARTITION_OFFSET(boot_partition)
only describes one of them.

With CONFIG_ESP_C6_OTA_BOOT_PROBE, call a hook provided by the
application/BSP that resolves the actual partition offset at runtime
(otadata decode + image scan fallback). Without the option, behavior is
unchanged.
---
 soc/espressif/common/loader.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/soc/espressif/common/loader.c b/soc/espressif/common/loader.c
index 000000000..000000001 100644
--- a/soc/espressif/common/loader.c
+++ b/soc/espressif/common/loader.c
@@ -139,7 +139,16 @@ void map_rom_segments(int core, struct rom_segments *map)
 	/* Traverse segments to fix flash offset changes due to post-build processing */
 #ifndef CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT
 	esp_image_segment_header_t WORD_ALIGNED_ATTR segment_hdr;
+#if defined(CONFIG_ESP_C6_OTA_BOOT_PROBE)
+	/*
+	 * The image may live in either OTA slot; let the platform resolve
+	 * the actual flash offset (otadata + image scan) at runtime.
+	 */
+	uint32_t esp_c6_boot_image_offset(void);
+	size_t offset = esp_c6_boot_image_offset();
+#else
 	size_t offset = PARTITION_OFFSET(boot_partition);
+#endif
 	bool checksum = false;
 	unsigned int segments = 0;
 	unsigned int ram_segments = 0;
-- 
